                                "sense_id": "b1d6a262-18ad-3828-bc3e-a451e304bca9",
                                "text": "The other half of the local staff was employed as interpreters, often affectionately known as 'interrupters.'"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c45e8434-9c18-4b98-a587-c4b8716169e7",
                                "sense_id": "b1d6a262-18ad-3828-bc3e-a451e304bca9",
                                "text": "The Coldstream Guards were already in place and knocked on the door. Daz Farrugia stood at the door with the Iraqi interrupter. […] The door opened and a middle aged Iraqi man stood there in his pajamas, gobbing off in Arabic, saying who knows what, but I guessed it was not very complimentary; the interpreter managed to calm him down."
                            }
                        ]
